**`app/controllers/general.php` line 809 — routing comparison semantics.**
```php
$host = $request->getHostname() ?? '';
$mainDomain = System::getEnv('_APP_CONSOLE_DOMAIN', System::getEnv('_APP_DOMAIN', ''));
// Only run Router when external domain
if ($host !== $mainDomain || !empty($previewHostname)) {
```
This is a behavioral concern. Previously `_APP_DOMAIN` was the domain used to decide whether the request host matches the "main domain" (i.e., the console). Now it's `_APP_CONSOLE_DOMAIN`. Note this is a *different* semantic role than the others — this one is a *comparison against a request host* to decide whether to route to the console or to the external domain router. There is a subtle issue: `_APP_CONSOLE_DOMAIN` falling back to `_APP_DOMAIN` — but if a deploy sets `_APP_CONSOLE_DOMAIN` to a *different* value than `_APP_DOMAIN`, then the console will be served at `_APP_CONSOLE_DOMAIN`, and the routing at line 809 must be in sync. This coupling holds as long as the fallback is uniform, which it is. OK.

